information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies general information in short written or spoken conversations."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "heartburn"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a burning feeling in your stomach or chest caused by acid from your stomach"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: That soup was too spicy! I have heartburn!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob07aud05"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about health problems."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "ginger tea"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a hot liquid made from ginger"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Ginger tea helps with heartburn."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob07aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to absorb"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to take in a liquid, gas"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The tea absorbs the acid in your stomach."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob07aud08"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to steep"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to put something in a liquid and leave it there"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Steep the ginger in boiling water."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob07aud10"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "calm your nerves"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "use to say someone should relax and not worry "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(expression)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Drink this; it helps calm your nerves."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob07aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to contribute"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to help make something happen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Your nerves contribute to heartburn."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob07aud09"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "freshly"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "when food is not preserved"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Add one spoon of freshly ground pepper."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob07aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "grated"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "in small pieces"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Is this grated ginger?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob07aud04"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "herbal"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "made of herbs"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Herbal teas help with many health issues."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob07aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "teaspoon "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a small spoon that you use for measuring food or liquid"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You must add one teaspoon of honey."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn4le16ob07aud07"}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn4le16ob07re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Talking About Health Problems "}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Explaining a problem</span> <br/> You can use these sentences to describe your health problems:<br/> <span class=\"bullet\"> I am not feeling well. / I don't feel well.</span><br/> <span class=\"bullet\"> I have a cough.</span><br/> <span class=\"bullet\"> I have a stomach ache.</span><br/> <span class=\"bullet\"> I have heartburn.</span><br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Symptoms</span><br/> Symptoms are feelings of illness or discomfort. <br/><br/>  <span class=\"strong\">Diagnosis</span><br/> A diagnosis is when a doctor tells you the medical name of your problem."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Must vs. Should"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use the modals <span class=\"italic\">must</span> and <span class=\"italic\">should</span> to give recommendations."}, {"type": "example", "content": "You must drink some tea. <br/> You have to drink lots of herbal tea. <br/> You should add one teaspoon of sugar. <br/>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Must</span> is a very strong recommendation. You can use <span class=\"strong\">have to</span> instead of must. <span class=\"strong\">Have to</span> is used as a strong obligation.<br/> <br/>  <span class=\"strong\">Should</span> is not as strong. It is a suggestion."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Read this list of common health problems:<ul> <li>food allergy</li><li>hay fever</li> <li>insomnia</li></ul>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Choose one of these. Do some research about it."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Fill in the table."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write down suggestions and strong recommendations about what someone should do if they have this problem."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share your table with a partner."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You must ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You should\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"&nbsp; <br/>&nbsp;\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research a common health problem."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I make suggestions and strong recommendations."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I organize my information in a table."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my table with a partner."}]}], "type": "sena"}